Categorical Lift Engine (CLE)
Copyright 2026 Gemmina Intelligence LLC.

This product includes software developed at Gemmina Intelligence LLC.

Categorical Lift Engine (CLE) is an optional knowledge-generation extension
of SensOS. It sits downstream of Meaning Space Runtime
(https://github.com/GemminAI/meaning-space-runtime) and upstream of HEKB,
and imports no code from either — it is structurally independent, wired
through Protocol-typed ports and frozen ABI values, the same convention
MSR and Meaning Mapper already establish.

The SensOS OSS stack (semantic-annotator-core, Meaning Mapper, Meaning
Space Runtime — all Apache-2.0) is complete and fully functional without
this repository: observation, measurement, meaning-state tracking, runtime
dynamics, and LLM-rendering integration all work with no dependency on
CLE. Installing CLE extends that stack by turning stabilized semantic
trajectories into reusable knowledge; it does not complete it.

This repository's inclusion outside the current OSS distribution is a
product-strategy decision, not a technical limitation. See LICENSE —
